Description: project templates: build through the V\OS makefile-engine
 The template compile scripts were raw gcc one-liners against the legacy
 toolchain, one of them assembled an .hpkg package, and the template
 project files carried legacy absolute paths and legacy-only support
 libraries. The scripts now generate a makefile-engine Makefile and run
 make, so a template build gets the system flag set, libroot and the
 engine's shared-object handling. The kernel driver template and the
 driver stub the template bootstrap used to generate are dropped as
 legacy-only.
Author: VitruvianOS Ports <ports@vitruvian.invalid>
Forwarded: no
Origin: upstream https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Paladin @ 5b7c442bd68eb3e04ce2b5b780eb2314db3b977a

